        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Section 7. Voluntary Rehabilitation.",
            "block_bbox": [
                105,
                436,
                463,
                461
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    105.0,
                    436.0
                ],
                [
                    463.0,
                    436.0
                ],
                [
                    463.0,
                    461.0
                ],
                [
                    105.0,
                    461.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a. The primary objectives of the Agency's drug and alcohol policy are to maintain employee performance and good health and a safe work environment. If, prior to a requirement by the Agency that the employee submit to any of the tests specified in Section 5 of this Article, the employee notifies a supervisor he or she has drug or alcohol problems that require treatment, then in that event the employee shall immediately submit to a medical evaluation by a doctor selected and paid for by the Agency and shall enroll in a treatment program recommended by the doctor. An employee may seek such evaluation and treatment from the employee's own doctor, at the employee's expense. The employee shall notify the employer of the name of the doctor. An employee who enters rehabilitation and successfully completes rehabilitation under the terms of this paragraph shall not be subject to discipline. The cost of such treatment shall be at the employee's expense except as it may be covered by insurance. The employee may take paid leave or leave without pay for the period of treatment.",
            "block_bbox": [
                104,
                463,
                1118,
                740
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    104.0,
                    463.0
                ],
                [
                    1118.0,
                    463.0
                ],
                [
                    1118.0,
                    740.0
                ],
                [
                    104.0,
                    740.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "b. If an employee has previously enrolled in a voluntary rehabilitative treatment described in subsection a and subsequently again volunteers for such treatment in advance of being required to submit to any of these tests specified in Section 5 of this Article, then the employee shall immediately submit to a medical evaluation by a doctor selected and paid for by the Agency and shall successfully complete the treatment program recommended by the doctor. An employee may seek such evaluation and treatment from the employee's own doctor, at the employee's expense. The employee shall notify the employer of the name of the doctor. If the employee fails to complete the treatment program successfully, he or she shall be subject to discipline up to and including termination. The cost of such treatment shall be at the employee's expense except as it may be covered by insurance. The employee may take paid leave or leave without pay for the period of treatment.",
            "block_bbox": [
                104,
                740,
                1118,
                994
            ],
